WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.289
At Christmas, the little village was cheerful.

2
00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:07.784
The weather was wild and cold.

3
00:00:07.785 --> 00:00:12.151
The snow was six feet deep and frozen hard.

4
00:00:12.152 --> 00:00:17.175
Despite all, the villagers smiled and were happy.

5
00:00:17.176 --> 00:00:20.913
Bells jingled on horses in the street.

6
00:00:20.914 --> 00:00:25.547
Every house in the village was decorated for Christmas.

7
00:00:25.548 --> 00:00:29.364
Cakes and candy were given as gifts.

8
00:00:29.365 --> 00:00:33.619
Friends gathered in homes for joking and dancing.

9
00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:39.598
Pots full of soup sat on the stoves.

10
00:00:39.599 --> 00:00:43.707
It was dark and sad only in the little hut.

11
00:00:43.708 --> 00:00:48.938
A week before Christmas, Death entered the tiny home.

12
00:00:48.939 --> 00:00:56.606
Jehan, Nello's loving grandfather and Patrasche's caring owner, passed away.

13
00:00:56.607 --> 00:01:01.586
Nello and Pastrasche were left utterly alone.

14
00:01:01.587 --> 00:01:07.717
Jehan had been sick for a long time, spending his days in bed.

15
00:01:07.718 --> 00:01:14.749
He hadn't spoken for many weeks, but he had always smiled for Nello and Patrasche.

16
00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:19.010
His loss gave them both great grief.

17
00:01:19.011 --> 00:01:24.762
Nello and Patrasche stayed with Jehan's body all day in the hut.

18
00:01:24.763 --> 00:01:32.235
The next afternoon, his coffin was taken to an unmarked grave by the little gray church.

19
00:01:32.236 --> 00:01:36.848
Nello and Patrasche were the only mourners.

20
00:01:36.849 --> 00:01:43.924
The miller's wife saw Nello and Patrasche walking behind the coffin on the way to the church.

21
00:01:43.925 --> 00:01:48.058
"Surely, my husband will change his mind about Nello.

22
00:01:48.059 --> 00:01:51.502
He will let Nello see Alois,"

23
00:01:51.503 --> 00:01:55.397
she thought, looking at Master Cogez.

24
00:01:55.398 --> 00:02:00.312
The miller knew her thought, but he would not change his mind.

25
00:02:00.313 --> 00:02:04.835
"The boy is a beggar," he said to himself.

26
00:02:04.836 --> 00:02:08.439
"He should not be friends with Alois."

27
00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:13.127
The miller's wife did not dare say anything aloud.

28
00:02:13.128 --> 00:02:20.936
But after Nello and Patrasche had left the grave, she put some flowers into Alois' hands.

29
00:02:20.937 --> 00:02:27.210
She told Alois to take the flowers and place them on Jehan's grave.

30
00:02:27.211 --> 00:02:31.852
Nello and Patrasche went home with broken hearts.

31
00:02:31.853 --> 00:02:36.770
When they got home, a small note was nailed to the door.

32
00:02:36.771 --> 00:02:38.771
Nello read it.

33
00:02:38.772 --> 00:02:44.665
It said the rent for the little hut was overdue.

34
00:02:44.666 --> 00:02:50.797
The owner of the hut was a farmer and also a friend of Master Cogez.

35
00:02:50.798 --> 00:02:55.682
Nello slowly walked down the road to the farmer's house.

36
00:02:55.683 --> 00:03:01.692
After he had paid for the funeral, Nello had no money left.

37
00:03:01.693 --> 00:03:06.766
The farmer answered the door with an annoyed look on his face.

38
00:03:06.767 --> 00:03:11.089
He listened to Nello explain his situation.

39
00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:14.357
The farmer's look did not change.

40
00:03:14.358 --> 00:03:22.481
He told Nello he wanted everything in the hut as payment for the rent ─ every pot and pan.

41
00:03:22.482 --> 00:03:28.808
Then the farmer told Nello and Patrasche to be out of the hut by the next day.

42
00:03:28.809 --> 00:03:34.185
Nello begged the farmer to change his mind, but he wouldn't listen.

43
00:03:34.186 --> 00:03:40.549
The farmer began to shout, and Nello turned with Patrasche to leave.

44
00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:46.158
The hut was only a simple home, but they had been happy there.

45
00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:50.308
In the summer, the hut was pretty and bright.

46
00:03:50.309 --> 00:03:53.883
The garden had given them vegetables.

47
00:03:53.884 --> 00:03:58.505
In the shed, Nello had drawn his pictures.

48
00:03:58.506 --> 00:04:05.826
All night long, the boy and the dog sat in the hut, without a fire to keep them warm.

49
00:04:05.827 --> 00:04:08.563
They slept close together.

50
00:04:08.564 --> 00:04:17.771
Nello and Patrasche had nothing left but each other.

